<article>

<h1>$ifdef(censored)$Suppressed $endif$Comment</h1>

$ifdef(censored)--$
<div class="notecard warning markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning">
<p><strong>Censored:</strong> This comment or one of its ancestors was suppressed.  It has been torn out of the Open&nbsp;Web:  It is invisible to search engines, archivers, and people who disable JavaScript, and it cannot be directly referenced via the Web’s core feature:  A direct hyperlink.  To see the comment, user interaction with JavaScript enabled.</p>
</div>

$endif--$
<ul>
$ifdef(Title)--$
<li><strong>Subject:</strong> $Title.escapehtml$</li>$endif--$
$ifdef(Author)--$
<li><strong>Author:</strong> $Author.escapehtml$</li>$endif--$
$ifdef(Time)--$
<li><strong>Timestamp:</strong> <time datetime="$Time.escapehtml$" title="$Time.escapehtml$">$Time.escapehtml$$ifdef(Server-Time)$ (server time: “$Server-Time.escapehtml$”)$endif$</time></li>$endif--$<!-- time -->
$for(archive.split)--$
<li><strong>Archive:</strong> <a href="$this.escapehtmlurl$">$this.escapehtml$</a></li>
$endfor--$
$ifdef(URL)--$
<li><strong>URL:</strong> <a href="$URL.escapehtmlurl$">$URL.escapehtml$</a></li>$endif--$
$ifdef(IRT-Author)--$
<li><strong>In-Reply-To:</strong> $ifdef(IRT-URL)--$
<a href="$IRT-URL.escapehtmlurl$">$endif--$
$ifdef(IRT-Author)--$<!-- XXX redundant, but control statements lack sufficient flexibility to make the outer $ifdef$ do what I want. -->
$IRT-Author.escapehtml$$endif--$
$ifdef(IRT-TS)$ <time datetime="$IRT-TS.escapehtml$">$IRT-TS.escapehtml$</time>$endif--$
$ifdef(IRT-URL)$</a>$endif--$
</li>$endif--$<!-- In-Reply-To -->
$ifdef(Ed-Note)--$
<li><strong>Editor’s Note:</strong> $Ed-Note$</li>$endif--$

</ul>

$body$
</article>
